<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Four tiered forest materials (技术/02-魔法实现.md, 「四阶专属材料面板草案」, 2026-11-13).

    Columns are carried one by one onto vanilla fields:
      质量            -> Mass
      锐伤倍率        -> SharpDamageMultiplier
      钝伤倍率        -> BluntDamageMultiplier
      近战攻速系数    -> stuffProps/statFactors/MeleeWeapon_CooldownMultiplier
      锐甲/钝甲/热甲  -> StuffPower_Armor_Sharp/Blunt/Heat

    The staff reads the armour columns back out of the material instead of keeping its own table
    (SpellStaffModifiers.cs: blunt armour lowers the mana cost, heat armour lengthens effects,
    the sharp/blunt damage average raises damage).

    Category and flammability are fixed by the brief: living wood is Woody at 0.2, the three
    metals are Metallic and do not burn; adamantine and mithril keep a melee cooldown factor of 1.

    Not carried here, for want of a vanilla stuff field (reported in the handoff):
      * mithril's two reaction slots and its x0.70 reaction-spell mana cost (spell injection system);
      * living wood's ranged-cooldown bonus for the elven longbow (the table gives no value).

    No acquisition path on purpose: point-transmutation arrives with the altar tiers, so these are
    Lab-spawnable only for now.

    Placeholder art: every texPath borrows the mod's own chalk texture, tinted per material, until
    the M1-M4 stack-count art in 技术/09-美术资产清单 exists. The table asks for Graphic_StackCount,
    which needs a folder of three images, so the placeholder is Graphic_Single.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>WotF_LivingWood</defName>
    <label>living wood</label>
    <description>Living wood cut from the forest's oldest trees. It is still growing: flexible, warm to the touch and slow to burn.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Chalk</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <color>(122,160,92)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Wood_Drop</soundInteract>
    <soundDrop>Wood_Drop</soundDrop>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>0.30</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.2</Flammability>
      <StuffPower_Armor_Sharp>0.72</StuffPower_Armor_Sharp>
      <StuffPower_Armor_Blunt>0.75</StuffPower_Armor_Blunt>
      <StuffPower_Armor_Heat>0.60</StuffPower_Armor_Heat>
      <SharpDamageMultiplier>0.75</SharpDamageMultiplier>
      <BluntDamageMultiplier>1.05</BluntDamageMultiplier>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <burnableByRecipe>true</burnableByRecipe>
    <healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
    <stuffProps>
      <categories>
        <li>Woody</li>
      </categories>
      <commonality>0</commonality>
      <allowedInStuffGeneration>false</allowedInStuffGeneration>
      <appearance>Planks</appearance>
      <constructEffect>ConstructWood</constructEffect>
      <color>(122,160,92)</color>
      <soundImpactBullet>BulletImpact_Wood</soundImpactBullet>
      <soundMeleeHitSharp>MeleeHit_Wood</soundMeleeHitSharp>
      <soundMeleeHitBlunt>MeleeHit_Wood</soundMeleeHitBlunt>
      <soundImpactMelee>Pawn_Melee_Punch_HitBuilding_Wood</soundImpactMelee>
      <statFactors>
        <Flammability>0.2</Flammability>
        <MeleeWeapon_CooldownMultiplier>0.95</MeleeWeapon_CooldownMultiplier>
      </statFactors>
    </stuffProps>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Light</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>WotF_ElvenSteel</defName>
    <label>elven steel</label>
